# MongoDB — REQUIRED in production for quote-form lead storage.
# Without it the form shows an honest error state instead of pretending to submit.
# Opcional: apunta staging a otra base para no contaminar leads reales.
# Si se omite, el codigo usa 305-web-service-db
# MONGODB_DB=305-web-service-db-staging
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://user:password@cluster.mongodb.net/305-web-service-db

# WhatsApp number for all "Chat on WhatsApp" CTAs. Digits only, incl. country code.
VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=13058332984

# Public contact email shown in the footer and contact page.
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=305webservice@gmail.com

# ── Analytics (OPTIONAL, not yet connected) ─────────────────────────────
# The site already fires conversion events via src/lib/analytics.ts:
#   hero_cta_primary, header_cta_click, package_cta_click, service_offer_cta,
#   problem_cta_click, final_cta_click, whatsapp_click, phone_click,
#   email_click, form_start, form_submit_success (+ selected service/budget).
# They no-op until a platform is present on window. To activate, add ONE of:
#   - Google Analytics 4 (gtag) snippet, or
#   - Plausible (window.plausible), or
#   - a dataLayer + GTM container.
# No personal information is sent to analytics. UTM/referrer are captured with
# the form submission (consent-gated) and stored with the lead, not sent to GA.

# ── Google Places API (OPTIONAL — digital-card reviews module) ───────────
# Server-side ONLY. Never expose this key to the client; the card fetches
# reviews through /api/card-reviews/<placeId>, which runs on the server.
# Restrict the key to the Places API (New) and to your production environment.
# Without it, the reviews module simply does not render (no fake data).
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# How to configure a business for reviews (src/data/card.ts → profile.reviews):
#   1. Find the Place ID: https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/places/web-service/place-id
#   2. Get the official "write a review" URL from the Google Business Profile
#      dashboard ("Ask for reviews" / "Get more reviews" short link).
#   3. Set enabled:true + placeId + requestReviewUrl. Both are required —
#      the module refuses to render with only one of them.
